---
/* A maintainer's note on a letter card, with a plot-stamp seal. */
---

<section class="letter-sec" id="about">
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="sheet-wrap">
      <article class="sheet">
        <p class="over">A LETTER</p>
        <h2>From the maintainer</h2>
        <p class="para">
          Studying with an agent shouldn't mean five browser tabs, hand-download
          PDFs, and copy-pasted forum threads. moodle-mcp started as a way to
          hand my own coursework agent the same access the official mobile app
          has — no scraping, no browser automation, just the web services
          Moodle already exposes.
        </p>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <p class="para">
          Everything ships in one static Rust binary: 22 typed tools, document
          conversion, and an auth CLI. Writes ask first, drafts come before
          finals, and quiz-taking stays out on purpose. If that trade sounds
          right to you, install it and ask your agent what's due.
        </p>
        <div class="sign">
          <img
            class="avatar"
            src="/brand/moodle-mcp-icon.svg"
            alt=""
            width="34"
            height="34"
          />
          <div>
            <p class="who">G36maid</p>
            <p class="sub">maintainer</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <svg class="stamp" viewBox="0 0 120 120" aria-hidden="true">
          <defs>
            <path id="circ" d="M60,60 m-44,0 a44,44 0 1,1 88,0 a44,44 0 1,1 -88,0" />
          </defs>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="54" fill="none" stroke="#f5c9a0" stroke-width="1.5" />
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="34" fill="none" stroke="#f5c9a0" stroke-width="1" />
          <text class="ring">
            <textPath href="#circ">SINGLE BINARY · MOODLE-MCP · EST 2025 · MIT ·</textPath>
          </text>
          <path
            d="M48 72v-20l10 12 2-8 2 8 10-12v20"
            fill="none"
            stroke="#f98012"
            stroke-width="3"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
        </svg>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .letter-sec {
    max-width: calc(var(--frame-max) + 2px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 56px var(--gutter);
  }

  .sheet-wrap {
    max-width: 980px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background:
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        45deg,
        rgba(19, 72, 220, 0.05) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 9px
      ),
      var(--paper-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px;
  }

  .sheet {
    position: relative;
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 88% 12%,
        rgba(19, 72, 220, 0.06),
        transparent 42%
      ),
      #fdfdfb;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 44px 48px 40px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .over {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 30px;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .para {
    max-width: 480px;
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .rule {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    width: 120px;
    margin: 26px 0 0;
  }

  .sign {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .avatar {
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .who {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }

  .sub {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .stamp {
    position: absolute;
    top: 34px;
    right: 40px;
    width: 128px;
    height: 128px;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .ring {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    fill: #d9995b;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .sheet {
      padding: 32px 24px;
    }

    .stamp {
      position: static;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
